                <pb facs="1068" n="972" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg972"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1898</hi></date>.
                        (Received 3.50 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Spanish Government have informed British ambassador, Madrid, that the whole of
                    the treaty of seventeen ninety-five is abrogated, but if the Government of the
                    United States will propose through British embassy an agreement embodying
                    conditions of article 13, Spanish Government will accept; agreement must be
                    limited to merchants.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
